SUMMARY -- PART II
==============================================================================
PART 5  S(4) = varpi/2 - W/(2 varpi), W = 3F2(3/4,3/4,1/2;3/2,3/2;1):
        VERIFIED-EXACT to 170 digits; W confirmed by two independent routes.
PART 6  k = 4 is the unique positive integer at which (a) the 3F2 has a
        resonant exponent pair at infinity and (b) the K-moment weight
        mu^{4/k-1}(2-mu^2)^{-2/k-1/2} is a rational function.  PROVED.
PART 7  live positive control pi S(3) over B1: PASS
        B2 calibration score 4/5 -- B2 cannot see weight-1 log relations, so
        no negative is claimed from it.  See the two companion scripts.
